            },
            "hints": [
              {
                "content": "Think about how energy moves through an ecosystem. What is the starting point for almost all food chains on Earth?",
                "images": {},
                "replace": false,
                "widgets": {}
              },
              {
                "content": "Remember that producers, like plants, are the first step in most food chains. They make their own food using a specific type of energy. What is that primary energy source?",
                "images": {},
                "replace": false,
                "widgets": {}
              },
              {
                "content": "Plants capture light energy from the sun and convert it into chemical energy through photosynthesis. This chemical energy is then passed on to the animals that eat the plants, and then to the animals that eat those animals, and so on. So, the ultimate source for the hawk's energy, tracing it back through its prey and the plants its prey consumed, is the sun.",
